{"title":"Tailfin Cooks Up “Slow Riding” Waxed Canvas Bikepacking Setup in its R&D Kitchen","link":"https://bikerumor.com/tailfin-cooks-up-slow-riding-waxed-canvas-bikepacking-setup-in-its-rd-kitchen/","date":1793275320000,"content":"<p><img src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-hero.jpeg\" width=\"1280\" height=\"853\" alt=\"(Photos / Tailfin)\" /></p>\n<p>Look, if you’re rocking a <a href=\"https://www.tailfin.cc/us/\" target=\"_blank\">Tailfin</a> bikepacking system on your steed, there’s a good chance you bikepack “fast” or “ultra”. Like, you need your bikepacking gear minimal and strapped high and tight on your bike. Well, recently, Tailfin teased us with some work they’ve been doing in their R&amp;D Kitchen that’s for the bikepackers out there who aren’t in a hurry to get to where they’re going.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-patches.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"853\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-patches.jpeg\" alt=\"Tailfin Prototype Waxed Canvas Bikepacking Bags patches\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-patches.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-patches-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-patches-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-patches-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-patches-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-patches-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Now, this is a one-off, prototype bag setup. And as of right now, it will <em>not</em> be going into production. So try not to get too excited.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-with-pannier-open-e1792777265934.jpeg\"><img width=\"1122\" height=\"657\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-with-pannier-open-e1792777265934.jpeg\" alt=\"Tailfin Prototype Waxed Canvas Bikepacking Bags with pannier open\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-with-pannier-open-e1792777265934.jpeg 1122w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-with-pannier-open-e1792777265934-297x174.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-with-pannier-open-e1792777265934-120x70.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-with-pannier-open-e1792777265934-768x450.jpeg 768w\" /></a><figcaption>That fender line, though. Sexy AF!</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>Slowing Things Down…</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Tailfin is best known for making <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/tailfin-journey-launches-new-durable-versatile-and-modular-alloy-adventure-rack/\" target=\"_blank\">bikepacking gear</a> lighter, faster, and generally more aero than your average sleeping bag. So it’s kinda cool that its latest project is about slowing down, bringing a fishing rod, and not being in any hurry.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-front-bag.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"853\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-front-bag.jpeg\" alt=\"Tailfin Prototype Waxed Canvas Bikepacking Bags front bag\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-front-bag.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-front-bag-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-front-bag-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-front-bag-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-front-bag-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-front-bag-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The project came out of Tailfin’s “R&amp;D Kitchen,” a couple-times-a-year side gig for Tailfin’s prototyping department. The workshop sits next to the kitchen at HQ, so therefore “R&amp;D Kitchen”. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-left.jpeg\"><img width=\"854\" height=\"1280\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-left.jpeg\" alt=\"Tailfin Prototype Waxed Canvas Bikepacking Bags left\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-left.jpeg 854w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-left-200x300.jpeg 200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-left-80x120.jpeg 80w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-left-768x1151.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-left-600x900.jpeg 600w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-right.jpeg\"><img width=\"1080\" height=\"1280\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-right.jpeg\" alt=\"Tailfin Prototype Waxed Canvas Bikepacking Bags right\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-right.jpeg 1080w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-right-253x300.jpeg 253w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-right-101x120.jpeg 101w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-right-768x910.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-right-759x900.jpeg 759w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The department’s day job is building prototypes for the R&amp;D Division, which is the brand’s group of ultra athletes. The Kitchen projects have no commercial target. They’re about experimenting and having fun. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-front-pannier.jpeg\"><img width=\"1024\" height=\"1280\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-front-pannier.jpeg\" alt=\"Tailfin Prototype Waxed Canvas Bikepacking Bags front pannier\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-front-pannier.jpeg 1024w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-front-pannier-240x300.jpeg 240w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-front-pannier-96x120.jpeg 96w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-front-pannier-768x960.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-front-pannier-720x900.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>For this one, the team skipped the usual “lighter and faster” goal. Instead, they asked what they’d actually want to take on a trip built around the stops rather than the distance. Their answer was extra time and extra luxuries. </p>\n\n\n\n<h2>For the Love of Waxed Canvas…</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The bags are the star here, as they should be. Product team member Theo designed a front bag designed around holding a film camera, complete with a pocket for a real paper map “for the romance of it.” So far, I love this…</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-seamstress.jpeg\"><img width=\"1024\" height=\"1280\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-seamstress.jpeg\" alt=\"Tailfin Prototype Waxed Canvas Bikepacking Bags seamstress\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-seamstress.jpeg 1024w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-seamstress-240x300.jpeg 240w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-seamstress-96x120.jpeg 96w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-seamstress-768x960.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-seamstress-720x900.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Molly turned one pannier into an insulated cool bag for cold beers and a refrigerated picnic. What? She also made a separate bag for a small espresso maker. This is turning out to be spectacular…</p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-left-gallery.jpeg\"><img width=\"853\" height=\"1280\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-left-gallery.jpeg\" alt=\"Tailfin Prototype Waxed Canvas Bikepacking Bags left gallery\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-left-gallery.jpeg 853w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-left-gallery-200x300.jpeg 200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-left-gallery-80x120.jpeg 80w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-left-gallery-768x1152.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-left-gallery-600x900.jpeg 600w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-right-gallery.jpeg\"><img width=\"853\" height=\"1280\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-right-gallery.jpeg\" alt=\"Tailfin Prototype Waxed Canvas Bikepacking Bags right gallery\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-right-gallery.jpeg 853w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-right-gallery-200x300.jpeg 200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-right-gallery-80x120.jpeg 80w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-right-gallery-768x1152.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-right-gallery-600x900.jpeg 600w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Soft Goods Prototyper Callum redesigned the frame bag with flip-top closures instead of zips. And it’s split vertically rather than horizontally, with access at the front so you can dig around in it while riding. </p>\n\n\n\n<h2>1960s Japanese Touring!</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The inspiration came from Callum’s research into 1960s Japanese touring photos, which led back to the French constructeurs, who built bikes, racks, and bags as one integrated system. Japanese builders refined the idea over the following decades. “The bags aren’t an afterthought,” Callum said. The result is a British take on that tradition.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>But what about the bike? The bags are built around the new Singular Peregrine Mk5, a lugged steel bike from Sam Alison’s Singular Cycles. Alison launched the Peregrine in 2008, and it was arguably a gravel bike before the category had a name. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-sweing.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"853\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-sweing.jpeg\" alt=\"Tailfin Prototype Waxed Canvas Bikepacking Bags sweing\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-sweing.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-sweing-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-sweing-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-sweing-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-sweing-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-sweing-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Tailfin made its own versions of two touring classics for it: low front panniers and a randonneur handlebar bag. Both use British waxed canvas that weathers naturally, plus the same mounting hardware and stability engineering as Tailfin’s race gear. Bristol tailor David Darby Minns, a friend of the team, supplied fabric samples and vintage tailoring inspiration.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>This bike and bag system hits me right in the feels so hard. The color, the aesthetics, the fenders… I am a sucker for a good-lookin’ randoneurring rig. But sadly, it’s not a product that’s in development. Boo!!!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-more-patches.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"853\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-more-patches.jpeg\" alt=\"Tailfin Prototype Waxed Canvas Bikepacking Bags more patches\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-more-patches.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-more-patches-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-more-patches-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-more-patches-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-more-patches-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Tailfin-Prototype-Waxed-Canvas-Bikepacking-Bags-more-patches-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a><figcaption>(Photos / Tailfin)</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>However, the light at the end of the tunnel is that Tailfin expects ideas from the project to inform future work. So, hopefully we will see some more waxed canvas. </p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Where to See It?</h2>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Kendal Mountain Festival, 19–22 November 2026, Kendal, UK.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Velofollies, 22–24 January 2027, Kortrijk Xpo, Belgium</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Hit the link below for Tailfin products that are in production and ready to go. </p>\n\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https://www.tailfin.cc/us/\">TailFin.cc</a></p>\n\n\n\n<p></p>","author":"Ron Frazelle","comments":"https://bikerumor.com/tailfin-cooks-up-slow-riding-waxed-canvas-bikepacking-setup-in-its-rd-kitchen/#respond","siteTitle":"Bikerumor","siteHash":"49f427af0a926f4232eb837006841d7242e153e3afbb590f32e4b104ea3e2718","entryHash":"404525b13d31f5acd819bdd7c665c63bfc9d9544c5884cab244e549dcdb7af28","category":"Cycling"}